> Some more thoughts I had for discussion of the thin-thread.=20
>  =20
> 1.  To create a vendor independent solution I thought we should come=20
> up with a virtual printer.  The I/O channel for the virtual printer=20
> would be the "display" otherwise it would be like any other printer. =20
> So someone (I was thinking Till would be good candidate) could come up
> a description for the virtual printer.  Since this is an embedded thin
> thread I don't think the printer is high-end or even office level.  =20
> Things that need to be defined are DPI, paper size support, input=20
> image types, etc.   The actual virtual printer driver would not really
> have a color-correction but could have dither/half-tone and color=20
> channels like any-other printer.   The output of the driver could rgb=20
> dithered data.=20
>  =20
> 2. I believe we also need to thin thread an application.  The question
> is what type of application.  I think this is something for the group=20
> to come up with ideas and features for.   I don't really have any=20
> super good ideas at the moment and I am completely open.    I do think
> the application should have both images and text; so it could a mini-
